  "-Um- and mag- verbs focus on the doer, and the verb usually comes first.",
  "-Um- goes in front of a vowel root (umalís) or after the first consonant (kumain).",
  "Mag- goes in front of the root, with a hyphen before a vowel (mag-áral); past and present use nag-.",
  "Present repeats the first syllable (kumakain, naglulutò); future too, without -um- (kakain) or with mag- (maglulutò).",
  "When a root takes both: -um- is casual or toward the doer (bumilí, buy); mag- is intense or away from the doer (magbilí, sell).",
  "Pattern 1: verb + doer + object (preferred with siyá, silá). Pattern 2: verb + object + doer."
